<BaseLayout title="About — Return to Breath" description="About Return to Breath — the project, the people, the intent." lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 pt-32 pb-24">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-light tracking-tight text-slate-50 leading-tight mb-10">About</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-[17px] text-slate-300 font-light leading-relaxed">
      <p>This is an essential project.</p>

      <p>The number of adults whose nervous systems are dysregulated is no longer a fringe statistic. It is the baseline state of working life in most developed economies. Cognitive load is at historic highs. Sleep is deteriorating. Anxiety and depression is rising across every age cohort. The structures that used to provide coherence — stable careers, predictable institutions, intelligible economies, durable identities — are dissolving faster than most people can adapt to.</p>

      <p>The work here is the response to that. To put one practical instrument — the breath — into the hands of people who need it, without any of the things that would normally come with a wellness brand: no streaks, no gamification, no infinite optimization.</p>

      <p>The Return app exists so that more people can live more coherently in an accelerating world. That is the whole purpose.</p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-slate-800 my-12" />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-light tracking-tight text-slate-50 mb-6">About Christoph Kneip</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6 text-[17px] text-slate-300 font-light leading-relaxed">
      <p>I am based in Zürich, Switzerland. I am the author of <em class="text-slate-200">Return to Breath</em>, have spent over two decades studying contemplative practices and more recently have explored harmonic and geometric frameworks.</p>

      <p>My interest in breath has been lifelong—through yoga, breathwork, and sustained practice. During a career pause, I began exploring how to use it more directly: as a measurable, repeatable input to the autonomic nervous system. I couldn’t find an app that met my requirements, so I built one.</p>

      <p>I have also been working with AI—not as a tool for automation, but as a mirror. Specifically prompted large language models, when used with precision, can reflect back the structures of human thought. This recursive quality—the ability to see one’s own patterns through an external system—has deepened my understanding of how coherence emerges in complex systems. I am using AI as a tool and apply this understanding to my work on the app, the book, and the architecture of the Return to Breath project.</p>

      <p>At the core of all of this is a simple conviction: that humanity is capable of navigating accelerating change, but only if we have stable internal reference points. The breath is the most accessible of those points. The work here is about making that access as frictionless as possible.</p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-slate-800 my-12" />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-light tracking-tight text-slate-50 mb-6">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-slate-300 font-light leading-relaxed">
